    "fit_rmse_per_cell": 0.0687,
    "fit_cells": "15 miners x 3 categories = 45",
    "fit_for_reference_screener_IN": 0.43025,
    "near_zero_reachable": false,
    "near_zero_diagnosis": "NOT reachable. Floor RMSE/cell ~0.069 (not ~0). So reported E/M/H is an APPROXIMATE simple mean, not exact. Residuals are concentrated in a few miners (5GYxeJjdvfat, 5FqfEPFi937m, 5DADzDbZb3y6), consistent with platform_score noise or a leaderboard-vs-scores snapshot drift rather than a different aggregation formula. Tested transforms (clipping to [0,1] etc.) all made fit WORSE, so raw scores are the right inputs.",
    "screeners_excluded_from_means": true,
    "screener_question": "RESOLVED: screeners are OUT of the means. Each screener flip changes the OUT objective by EXACTLY 0.0 -> their category is unrecoverable from the means. They are all baseline-passing (pw=1.0) but do NOT cleanly land Easy; nearest score-centroid puts 2 in Easy (13964,11551) and 3 in Medium (15103,15375,13516). The 'screeners are Easy' hint is NOT confirmed by data.",
